::STAT_U01_L04_GP_Q01::
Question ID: STAT_U01_L04_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.STQ.1
Question:
A survey records each student's favorite school lunch. Which display is appropriate?
{
~A. Histogram#A histogram is for numerical intervals, not category labels.
=B. Bar chart#A bar chart compares counts across lunch categories.
~C. Scatterplot#A scatterplot needs two numerical variables.
~D. Box plot#A box plot summarizes numerical data, not categories.
}

::STAT_U01_L04_GP_Q02::
Question ID: STAT_U01_L04_GP_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.STQ.1
Question:
Which display lists categories with the number of responses in each category?
{
~A. Scatterplot#A scatterplot shows paired numerical values.
~B. Histogram#A histogram groups numerical values into intervals.
=C. Frequency table#A frequency table organizes categories and counts.
~D. Dot plot#A dot plot shows one numerical variable.
}

::STAT_U01_L04_GP_Q03::
Question ID: STAT_U01_L04_GP_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.STQ.1
Question:
A school compares preferred study location by grade level. Which display organizes the two categorical variables?
{
=A. Two-way table#A two-way table organizes counts for combinations of two categorical variables.
~B. Histogram#A histogram is for one numerical variable.
~C. Box plot#A box plot summarizes a numerical distribution.
~D. Scatterplot#A scatterplot shows two numerical variables.
}

::STAT_U01_L04_GP_Q04::
Question ID: STAT_U01_L04_GP_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.STQ.1
Question:
A club wants to show the percent of members choosing each project type out of the whole club. Which display could fit?
{
~A. Scatterplot#A scatterplot is for two numerical variables.
~B. Histogram#A histogram shows numerical intervals.
~C. Box plot#A box plot summarizes numerical data.
=D. Pie chart#A pie chart can show how one categorical variable is divided into parts of a whole.
}

::STAT_U01_L04_GP_Q05::
Question ID: STAT_U01_L04_GP_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.STAT.STQ.1
Question:
Why is a histogram not appropriate for favorite music genre?
{
=A. Genre is categorical, so category counts should be shown with a bar chart or table#Histograms require numerical intervals, while genre names are categories.
~B. Genres are numerical measurements#Genres are labels, not measurements.
~C. Histograms are only for two variables#Histograms display one numerical variable.
~D. Music data can never be displayed#Music preferences can be displayed as categorical data.
}
